Applying the curve-type notation, the first triad (1-2-3) exhibits an increase followed by a decrease ($r_1 < r_2 > r_3$), corresponding to a K-type. The second triad (2-3-4) exhibits a continuous decrease ($r_2 > r_3 > r_4$), corresponding to a Q-type. Thus, the resulting curve type is KQ. This matches the classification currently on file.

